Data and derived figures

The MIT licence above covers the code. It does not cover data. No raw data is
redistributed in this repository; figures derived from data follow the terms of
their sources, recorded in data/MANIFEST.yaml and reference/source_checks.csv:

- Figures derived from the Jordà-Schularick-Taylor Macrohistory Database
  (Jordà et al. 2019, Quarterly Journal of Economics) are licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/): the historical return
  assumptions, the dividend-growth input and the validation statistics computed
  from it, wherever they appear (docs/, reports/, reference/upstream/, app/).
- Figures from MAS statistics and the MAS Survey of Professional Forecasters are
  used under the Monetary Authority of Singapore's Terms of Use of Datasets and
  carry its notice.
- Figures derived from sources with no stated licence (Robert Shiller's data, the
  Kenneth French data library, SingStat, Aswath Damodaran, the Philadelphia Fed
  Survey of Professional Forecasters) are summary statistics or cited figures only.
- Issuer, broker, IRAS and MOM documents are cited by figure and page and are not
  redistributed.
